# Bling API Reference Links

## Source of truth

Endpoints, parameters, and response shapes match the [Bling API v3 reference](https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia).

`README.md` records the aligned API revision (`v310`) and links to the [changelog](https://developer.bling.com.br/changelogs).

## `@see` on entity methods

Every entity method `@see` is the operation anchor, not only the resource section.

Copy the URL from a method on the same resource:

- `src/Entities/CamposCustomizados/CamposCustomizados.php` — custom fields
- `src/Entities/PedidosVendas/PedidosVendas.php` — orders and actions
- `src/Entities/Nfses/Nfses.php` — service invoices

The anchor's verb prefix (`get_`, `post_`, `put_`, `patch_`, `delete_`) selects `index`/`show`, `store`, `replace`, `update`, or `destroy`.

## Class-level `@see`

The class docblock links to the resource group (`#/Contatos`, `#/Campos%20Customizados`).

## README entity list

`README.md` keeps the consumer checklist of `$bling-><getter>` accessors. The getter text is the camelCase name from `Bling::__get`, including `formasDePagamentos`. Update the list when adding a module.

## Authentication docs

Point consumers to:

- `README.md` — `new Bling($accessToken)` and the note that this package does not run the OAuth grant
- `https://developer.bling.com.br/aplicativos#tokens-de-acesso`
- `demo/` — authorization-code sample that stores the token and calls `new Bling($accessToken)`

## Checks before adding an operation

1. Confirm the HTTP verb and path in the Bling reference.
2. Map the verb to `repository->*` (`architecture/repository-layer.mdc`).
3. Use the reference's Portuguese camelCase for query and body fields.
4. Add the operation `@see` with the encoded resource name and the operation anchor.

## Versioning

Package `1.x` (`composer.json` `version`) targets API v3. A breaking change in a Bling payload is applied by editing the `Schema/` classes of the affected operations.
